#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:77
msgid "Introduction to replica simulations"
msgstr "Replica シミュレーションの導入"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:79
msgid ""
"Many methods are based on the simultaneous simulation of multiple replicas. "
"In some cases, all the replicas will use the same input file, whereas in "
"other cases a separate input file should be provided for each replica. "
"Notice that using a single input file does not imply that all the replicas "
"will feel the same biasing potential. Biasing potentials in PLUMED might be "
"history dependent, and the history for one replica might differ from the "
"history for the other replicas, the potentials might, therefore, end up "
"being different."
msgstr ""
"多くの方法は、複数 Replica "
"の同時シミュレーションに基づきます。すべてに同じ入力を使う場合と、それぞれ別の入力を使う場合があります。入力が1つでも BiasPotential "
"が同じとは限りません。PLUMED の BiasPotential は履歴に依存する場合があり、Replica ごとに履歴が違えば Potential "
"も異なります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:81
msgid ""
"PLUMED has been designed so that multiple-replica simulations can be run "
"even if all the replicas are acting in the same directory. In order to avoid"
" clashes in output files, PLUMED will append a suffix corresponding to the "
"index of the replica to the name of each output file (for instance, the "
"command `PRINT FILE=colvar.dat` will print on a file names `colvar.0.dat` in"
" the first replica, etc.). Suffixes will be added also to input files, so "
"that if you run a simulation where the input file is `plumed.dat`, the first"
" replica will open a file named `plumed.0.dat`, and so on. However, for "
"input files, if the file including the suffix does not exist, PLUMED will "
"look for the file without the suffix (in the example the file called "
"`plumed.dat`). This provides maximum flexibility and allows to manage case "
"where the input file is the same for all replicas and cases where specific "
"and different input files should be used for each replica."
msgstr ""
"PLUMED は、全 Replica を同じディレクトリで実行できるよう設計されています。出力の衝突を避けるため、ファイル名に Replica "
"Index の接尾辞を付けます。例えば `PRINT FILE=colvar.dat` は最初の Replica で `colvar.0.dat` "
"を出力します。入力にも接尾辞を付け、`plumed.dat` を指定すると最初は `plumed.0.dat` "
"を開きます。ただし接尾辞付きの入力がなければ、接尾辞なしの `plumed.dat` を探します。これにより、全 Replica "
"共通の入力も、Replica ごとに異なる入力も柔軟に扱えます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:83
msgid ""
"In addition to this, it is possible to use a [special-replica-"
"syntax](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-doc/html/special-replica-"
"syntax.html) that allows one to use different inputs for the various "
"replicas even thought they all share the same `plumed.dat` file. For "
"instance, the command `RESTRAINT ARG=d AT=@replicas:1.0,1.1,1.2 KAPPA=1.0` "
"will apply restraints at different positions for the three replicas."
msgstr ""
"さらに [Special Replica Syntax](https://www.plumed.org/doc-master/user-"
"doc/html/special-replica-syntax.html) により、同じ `plumed.dat` を共有しながら Replica "
"ごとに異なる入力を指定できます。例えば `RESTRAINT ARG=d AT=@replicas:1.0,1.1,1.2 KAPPA=1.0` は、3"
" Replica の異なる位置に Restraint を加えます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:85
msgid ""
"Notice however that starting with GROMACS 2019 replica simulations are "
"forced to run in separate directories. To exploit the possibility to use a "
"single input file, one should put it in the parent directory and refer to is"
" as `-plumed ../plumed.dat`. Output files will be produced in separate "
"directories by default, but their names will be suffixed. If you want the "
"PLUMED output files to be in the parent directory, just prepend their name "
"with `../` (as in `PRINT FILE=../colvar.dat`)."
msgstr ""
"ただし GROMACS 2019以降では、Replica "
"は別ディレクトリで実行する必要があります。単一の入力を使うには親ディレクトリに置き、`-plumed ../plumed.dat` "
"で指定します。出力は既定では各ディレクトリに接尾辞付きで作られます。親ディレクトリに出したい場合は、名前に `../` を付けます（例：`PRINT "
"FILE=../colvar.dat`）。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:87
msgid ""
"In order to use multiple-replica methods, you should run your simulation "
"using MPI. This can be done prefixing your command with `mpiexec -np N "
"--oversubscribe`, where `N` is the number of processes that you want to use "
"and the `--oversubscribe` option is an OpenMPI option that is required to "
"use more processes than the number of available processors. This is "
"typically suboptimal, but we will need it in our lectures to run, e.g., "
"simulations with 32 replicas on a computer with 4 cores."
msgstr ""
"Multiple-replica 法には MPI が必要です。コマンドの前に `mpiexec -np N --oversubscribe` "
"を付けます。`N` は Process 数、`--oversubscribe` は Processor 数を超える Process を使うための "
"OpenMPI オプションです。通常は最適ではありませんが、この講義では4 Core の計算機で32 Replica を動かす場合などに必要です。"

