#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:172
msgid "Exercise 2: Demuxing your trajectories"
msgstr "演習2：Trajectory の Demux"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:174
msgid ""
"Close to the end of one of the `md.log` files produced by your simulation "
"you will find a short report that tells you about the accepted exchanges. "
"This report might look like this:"
msgstr "出力された `md.log` の1つの末尾近くに、受理された交換の短い報告があります。例えば次のようになります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:182
msgid ""
"A result like this one warns you that there is a bottleneck between replicas"
" 27 and 28 (only 1 percent of the attempted exchanges have been accepted). "
"Bottlenecks might be not visible in this representation, however. When it "
"comes to determining if there are bottlenecks the full path in the replica-"
"index space of the continuous trajectories (\"demuxed\") is much more "
"informative."
msgstr ""
"これは Replica 27と28の間に Bottleneck があることを示します。交換の試行の1%しか受理されていません。ただしこの表示では見えない"
" Bottleneck もあります。連続した「Demux 済み」Trajectory が Replica Index "
"空間で通る全経路を見る方が有用です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:185
msgid ""
"With this in mind we will now \"demux\" our trajectories. For these short "
"trajectories we can use the `demux.pl` script provided by GROMACS. Notice "
"that for long trajectories and frequent exchanges this script sometimes has "
"trouble processing the output file correctly. Trouble arrises because the "
"value of time is written by GROMACS with a limited number of digits. This "
"can make the original script confused about when exchanges happened. At "
"[this link](https://github.com/srnas/demux) you can find a modified script "
"that solves this problem by asking you the value of the time step. The new "
"script can then compute the value of time from the step number. As the step "
"number is stored as an integer and does not suffer roundoff problems."
msgstr ""
"そこで Trajectory を Demux します。短い Trajectory では GROMACS の `demux.pl` を使えます。ただし長い"
" Trajectory で交換頻度が高い場合、正しく処理できないことがあります。GROMACS "
"が時間を有限桁で出力するため、交換時刻の判定を誤ることが原因です。[こちら](https://github.com/srnas/demux) の改訂版は"
" Time Step を入力させ、整数で記録された Step 数から時間を求めるため、丸め誤差を避けられます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:188
msgid ""
"The demux script can be used to produce files named `replica_temp.xvg` and "
"`replica_index.xvg` by issuing the following command:"
msgstr ""
"次のコマンドで、Demux スクリプトから `replica_temp.xvg` と `replica_index.xvg` を生成します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:194
msgid ""
"The `replica_temp.xvg` files provides the number of the replica on which "
"each of the continuous simulations is located as a function of time. For "
"instance, you can follow the migration in the replica ladder of the first "
"replica by using the following python script:"
msgstr ""
"`replica_temp.xvg` は、各連続シミュレーションがどの Replica にいるかを時間の関数として示します。例えば次の Python "
"で、最初の Replica の Ladder 上の移動を追跡できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:201
msgid ""
"Column 1 contains the time, whereas the number on column i+1 tells you the "
"the current replica index (that is: temperature, in a temperature replica "
"exchange simulation; position of the restraint in a replica-exchange "
"umbrella sampling simulation) for the continuous simulation that started at "
"position i. This file is called \"replica_temp\" because it has been "
"implemented with temperature replica exchange in mind, but here the index "
"actually refers to the position of the restraint."
msgstr ""
"第1列は時間、第 i+1 列は位置 i から始まった連続シミュレーションの現在の Replica Index です。温度 Replica "
"Exchange なら温度、Replica Exchange Umbrella Sampling なら Restraint "
"の位置に対応します。温度交換を想定して実装されたため「replica_temp」という名前ですが、ここでは Restraint の位置です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:204 INSTRUCTIONS.md:217
msgid "Now answer the following two questions:"
msgstr "次の2点に答えてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:205
msgid "Does any replica explore the full range of indexes?"
msgstr "Index の全範囲を探索する Replica はありますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:206
msgid ""
"Are all the continuous replicas able to explore the full range of indexes?"
msgstr "すべての連続 Replica が Index の全範囲を探索できますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:208
msgid ""
"Notice that each row of the `replica_temp.xvg` file contains a permutation. "
"The `replica_index.xvg` file just contains the inverse of this permutation. "
"The `replica_index.xvg` can be used to generate the \"demuxed\" (continuous)"
" trajectories with the following command:"
msgstr ""
"`replica_temp.xvg` の各行は置換で、`replica_index.xvg` はその逆置換です。`replica_index.xvg` "
"を使い、次のコマンドで連続した Demux 済み Trajectory を生成できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:215
msgid ""
"The resulting trajectories can be visualized or analyzed as usual and, at "
"variance with the original trajectories, will have no jumps or "
"discontinuities. They are instead continuous functions of time. You can thus"
" use `plumed driver` to compute phi on the demuxed trajectories."
msgstr ""
"結果は通常どおり可視化・解析でき、元の Trajectory と違って Jump や不連続がありません。時間の連続関数なので、`plumed "
"driver` で phi を計算できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:218
msgid ""
"Does any replica jump from the metastable state at negative phi to the one "
"at positive phi (or viceversa)?"
msgstr "負の phi の準安定状態から正の phi の状態へ（または逆へ）移る Replica はありますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:219
msgid "Are all the continuous replicas able to do so?"
msgstr "すべての連続 Replica が移れますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:220
msgid "Are these two questions related to the two questions above?"
msgstr "この2点は、上の2点と関係しますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:222
msgid ""
"Notice that, if you run your simulation long enough, each \"demuxed\" "
"trajectory is expected to uniformly cover the full range of replica indexes."
" Due to the location of the restraints, this will imply that each "
"\"demuxed\" trajectory is expected to cover in an approximately uniform "
"manner the range of the biased CV. Each of these trajectories should, to a "
"certain extent, behave similarly to a metadynamics simulation. However, the "
"flatness of the distribution on the biased CV depends on the specific "
"parameters of the restraints (stiffness and locations)."
msgstr ""
"十分長く実行すれば、各 Demux 済み Trajectory は Replica Index "
"の全範囲を一様に探索すると期待されます。Restraint の位置から、Bias を加えた CV の範囲もほぼ一様に探索するはずです。各 "
"Trajectory は、ある程度 Metadynamics に似た挙動を示します。ただし CV 分布の平坦さは、Restraint "
"の強さと位置に依存します。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:224
msgid "Exercise 3: Block analysis from demuxed trajectories"
msgstr "演習3：Demux 済み Trajectory の Block Analysis"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:226
msgid ""
"Notice that the WHAM analysis does not need to know where each of the frames"
" come from. This implies that when you run WHAM you can do it equivalently "
"using the concatenation of the original trajectories or the concatenation of"
" the \"demuxed\" trajectories. The advantage of the latter choice is that "
"you can then perform a block analysis on the resulting trajectory where the "
"number of blocks is exactly equal to the number of replicas. These blocks "
"will be independent simulation, with only two small exceptions:"
msgstr ""
"WHAM は各 Frame の由来を必要としません。そのため元の Trajectory を連結しても、Demux "
"済みを連結しても等価です。後者では、Replica 数と同じ Block 数で Block Analysis ができます。各 Block "
"は独立したシミュレーションですが、小さな例外が2つあります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:228
msgid ""
"the paths in replica space are partly constrained, since when a replica goes"
" up another replica goes down."
msgstr "1つの Replica が上がると別のものが下がるため、Replica 空間の経路には部分的な制約がある。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:229
msgid ""
"replicas might be initialized from correlated conformations (e.g., all of "
"them in A), inducing a correlation."
msgstr "全 Replica を A に置くなど、相関した Conformation で初期化すると相関が生じる。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:231
msgid ""
"The second factor can be decreased by improving the way replicas are "
"initialized. The first factor usually impacts the correlation much less than"
" the actual exchanges. These blocks are thus optimally suited to perform a "
"bootstrap analysis of the error without incurring any underestimation due to"
" correlations between blocks."
msgstr ""
"後者は初期化方法の改善で減らせます。前者の影響は通常、実際の交換による相関よりはるかに小さくなります。この Block は、Block "
"間相関による過小評価を避けて Bootstrap で誤差を解析するのに適しています。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:233
msgid ""
"There is a small tricky issue here. When we perform the bootstrap analysis, "
"we are going to pick each block a different number of times. Since each "
"block (that is: each \"demuxed\" trajectory) has been spanning the replica "
"indexes by spending a different time at each replica, the bootstrap "
"trajectory will no longer spend the same time in each replica. The included "
"wham script allows to use this information passing an additional option "
"`traj_weight`. You can adjust the script below to perform the bootstrap "
"analysis:"
msgstr ""
"少し注意が必要です。Bootstrap では各 Block を異なる回数だけ選びます。各 Block（Demux 済み Trajectory）は "
"Replica ごとに異なる時間を過ごすため、Bootstrap Trajectory は各 Replica に同じ時間だけ滞在しません。付属の "
"WHAM スクリプトは `traj_weight` でこの情報を渡せます。次を変更して Bootstrap 解析してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:273
msgid ""
"Notice that this approach is not really standard, so use it with care. There"
" are a few papers in the literature discussing similar ideas, but they "
"usually require estimating the autocorrelation time in advance."
msgstr ""
"この方法は標準的とはいえないため、慎重に使ってください。類似の考え方を扱う論文はありますが、通常は事前に Autocorrelation Time "
"を推定する必要があります。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:275
msgid "Exercise 4: Bias-exchange metadynamics"
msgstr "演習4：Bias-exchange Metadynamics"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:277
msgid ""
"We will now run a bias-exchange simulation of alanine dipeptide. In bias-"
"exchange simulations, each replica biases a different collective variable. "
"This is a very practical way to enhance sampling for a large number of "
"variables (as many as the replicas that you can afford!). Notice that they "
"will be biased one at a time. As a matter of fact only those that are useful"
" in identifying a transition state will help, but the other ones will not "
"hurt."
msgstr ""
"次に Alanine Dipeptide の Bias-exchange を行います。各 Replica が異なる Collective "
"Variable に Bias を加える方法で、多数の変数（使える Replica 数まで）の Sampling を強化する実用的な方法です。各変数への"
" Bias は一度に1つずつです。Transition State の特定に有用な変数だけが役立ちますが、ほかの変数も悪影響は与えません。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:279
msgid ""
"Prepare the input file for a simulation with 3 replicas where the following "
"variables are biased:"
msgstr "次の変数に Bias を加える3 Replica の入力を用意してください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:280
msgid "`phi`"
msgstr "`phi`"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:281
msgid "`psi`"
msgstr "`psi`"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:282
msgid "none of them"
msgstr "どれにも加えない。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:284
msgid ""
"Initialize two of the replicas in structure A (using topolA.tpr) and one of "
"the replicas is structure B (using topolB.tpr). Notice that for plumed you "
"can use a single input file that looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"2 Replica は構造 A (topolA.tpr)、1 Replica は構造 B (topolB.tpr) で初期化します。plumed "
"は次のように単一の入力を使えます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:309
msgid ""
"Now run two separate simulations for 1000000 steps per replica. In one of "
"them you will propose exchanges between replicas with a pace 200, in the "
"other you will not propose any exchange (just omit `-replex 200` from the "
"command line). The second run will thus be equivalent to running three "
"simulations (free, metadynamics on phi, metadynamics on psi)."
msgstr ""
"各 Replica を1000000 Step 実行する2つのシミュレーションを行います。一方は200 Step "
"ごとに交換を試み、他方は交換しません（コマンドから `-replex 200` を省略）。後者は、Bias なし、phi の "
"Metadynamics、psi の Metadynamics の3本を実行するのと等価です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:311
msgid ""
"We will now use WHAM to combine the resulting trajectories. We can proceed "
"as we did above, but need to take account of the fact that when analyzing a "
"metadynamics simulations the way the weight is computed is slightly "
"different. As discussed in other masterclasses, one of the possible ways of "
"obtaining the weight is to use the final potential computed along the "
"trajectory. This requires a further processing step when doing a simple "
"metadynamics simulation. However, here we can compute the final potential "
"while processing the concatenated trajectory. In practice, you simply need "
"to use a plumed input file, where `PACE` has been set to a large number and "
"`HEIGHT` set to zero. You can then perform WHAM in the normal way and hence "
"compute the populations of the two metastable states."
msgstr ""
"WHAM で結果を統合します。上記と同様にできますが、Metadynamics では重みの計算法が少し異なります。ほかの Masterclass "
"で説明した方法の1つは、最終 Potential を Trajectory 上で評価することです。通常の Metadynamics "
"では追加処理が必要ですが、ここでは連結 Trajectory の処理中に計算できます。入力の `PACE` を大きく、`HEIGHT` "
"を0にするだけです。その後は通常どおり WHAM を行い、2つの準安定状態の Population を求められます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:313
msgid ""
"After you have calculated the relative populations in the two runs (with and"
" without exchanges), answer the following questions:"
msgstr "交換あり・なしの相対 Population を計算し、次に答えてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:315
msgid ""
"Is the relative population you obtain from the simulation with exchances "
"consistent with what you obtained from metadynamics simulations with no "
"exchanges?"
msgstr "交換ありの結果は、交換なしの Metadynamics で得た結果と整合しますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:316
msgid ""
"Are the two simulations (with exchanges and without exchanges) consistent "
"with each other?"
msgstr "交換あり・なしの2つのシミュレーションは互いに整合しますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:318
msgid ""
"Notice that the third replica has been simulated without any metadynamics. "
"This is a so-called neutral replica, that is sometimes used in bias-exchange"
" simulations. You can compute the relative population of the two metastable "
"states directly using the populations in that replica (no post-processing "
"needed!)."
msgstr ""
"3番目の Replica には Metadynamics を加えていません。Bias-exchange で使われることがある Neutral "
"Replica です。この Replica の Population から、後処理なしで2状態の相対 Population を直接計算できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:320
msgid ""
"Is the result you obtain from this analysis the same as that you obtain when"
" you use WHAM with all replicas?"
msgstr "この解析は、全 Replica を WHAM に使う場合と同じ結果になりますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:322
msgid ""
"Now imagine performing the bias-exchange simulation again usign only two "
"replicas: one of them biasing psi and the other one with no bias. In other "
"words, you would forget a variable on purpose that you know is very "
"important:"
msgstr ""
"次に2 Replica だけで Bias-exchange を行うとします。一方は psi に Bias、他方は Bias "
"なしです。重要だとわかっている変数を意図的に省きます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:324
msgid ""
"What do you expect will hapen to the resulting populations from this "
"simulation?"
msgstr "Population はどうなると予想しますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:326
msgid "Exercise 5: Parallel-tempering metadynamics"
msgstr "演習5：Parallel-tempering Metadynamics"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:328
msgid ""
"In these final two exercises We will learn how to use parallel-tempering "
"metadynamics. In parallel-tempering metadynamics, sampling is enhanced using"
" parallel-tempering (which enhances all degrees of freedom) and "
"metadynamics(which flattens the histogram for a few selected CVs). If the "
"biased CV contains a relevant bottleneck and is capable of approximately "
"singling out the corresponding transition state, the corresponding "
"transition will be enhanced as well. Notice however that if the parallel-"
"tempering side of the algorithm is sufficient to enhance sampling, it is not"
" necessary to bias a CV that can identify the transition state."
msgstr ""
"最後の2つの演習では Parallel-tempering Metadynamics を学びます。全自由度を強化する Parallel "
"Tempering と、少数の選択した CV の Histogram を平坦化する Metadynamics で Sampling を強化します。CV "
"が重要な Bottleneck を含み、対応する Transition State をおおよそ識別できれば、その遷移も強化されます。ただし "
"Parallel Tempering だけで十分な場合は、Transition State を識別する CV に Bias を加える必要はありません。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:330
msgid ""
"The first step will be to prepare our input files. We will use 4 replicas, "
"with temperatures taken from a geometric distribution ranging between 300 "
"and 800K. You should be able to generate the corresponding tpr files using "
"the following script"
msgstr "まず入力を用意します。300〜800 K の等比間隔の温度で4 Replica を使います。次のスクリプトで tpr を生成できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:354
msgid ""
"You will then be able to run a parallel tempering simulation with the "
"following command"
msgstr "次のコマンドで Parallel Tempering を実行できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:360
msgid ""
"Notice that the acceptance will be computed by GROMACS taking into account "
"the fact that simulations are running at different temperatures. Also notice"
" that in order to obtain a large enough acceptance given the temperature "
"span, you will need a number of replicas that grows with the square root of "
"the number of atoms in the system. For solvated molecules, you would "
"typically need tens of replicas at least."
msgstr ""
"GROMACS は温度の違いを考慮して受理率を計算します。この温度範囲で十分な受理率を得るには、系の原子数の平方根に比例する Replica "
"数が必要です。溶媒中の分子では通常、少なくとも数十 Replica が必要です。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:362
msgid ""
"We will now add the metadynamics ingredient, by preparing a suitable PLUMED "
"input file. Since parallel-tempering metadynamics is designed to cope with "
"cases where you do not have a good CV available, we will bias `psi` rather "
"than `phi`!"
msgstr ""
"適切な PLUMED 入力を作り、Metadynamics を加えます。この方法は適切な CV がない場合を想定しているので、`phi` ではなく "
"`psi` に Bias を加えます！"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:385
msgid ""
"The analysis will be simpler here. We will just analyze the first replica "
"(in `ptmetad_0`) as if it was generated using a simple metadynamics "
"simulation. Now compute the usual ratio between the populations of the two "
"metastable minima and answer the following questions:"
msgstr ""
"解析は簡単です。最初の Replica（`ptmetad_0`）を通常の Metadynamics として解析します。2つの準安定極小の "
"Population 比を計算し、次に答えてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:387
msgid ""
"Is the result compatible with what you obtained using umbrella sampling?"
msgstr "Umbrella Sampling の結果と整合しますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:388
msgid ""
"Was biasing psi useful in this case (you can also try to compute the "
"populations from a parallel tempering simulation without metadynamics to "
"answer this question)?"
msgstr ""
"psi に Bias を加えることは有用でしたか？Metadynamics なしの Parallel Tempering の Population "
"も計算すると判断できます。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:390
msgid "Exercise 6: Parallel-tempering: pathological case"
msgstr "演習6：Parallel Tempering の病的な例"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:392
msgid ""
"Repeat the previous exercise, but now place your replicas in the range "
"between 300 and 310 and answer the following questions."
msgstr "Replica の温度範囲を300〜310にして前の演習を繰り返し、次に答えてください。"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:394
msgid ""
"Is the population of the two states compatible with what you obtained in the"
" other exercises above."
msgstr "2状態の Population は、上のほかの演習の結果と整合しますか？"

#: INSTRUCTIONS.md:395
msgid ""
"If not, which is the correct answer? Draw some conclusion on how to detect "
"this type of problem in a realistic situation."
msgstr "整合しない場合、どれが正しいでしょうか？実際の状況でこの問題を検出する方法について考察してください。"
